$ unikraft certificate --help

stdout:
	Manage Unikraft Cloud certificates.

	Usage:
	  unikraft certificates <command> [flags]

	Commands:
	  get, inspect, show
	          Inspect a certificate.
	  wait
	          Wait for certificates to match a filter.
	  list, ls
	          List certificates.
	  delete, rm, remove
	          Remove a certificate.
	  create
	          Create a certificate.

	Fields:
	  metro
	  name
	  uuid
	  common-name
	  subject
	  issuer
	  serial-number
	  state
	  timestamps, timestamps.created, timestamps.not-before, timestamps.not-after
	  cn
	  chain
	  pkey

	Global flags:
	  -h, --help
	          Show context-sensitive help.
	      --config ($UNIKRAFT_CONFIG)
	          Path to the configuration file.
	      --log-level ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_LEVEL)
	          Set the logging level.
	          [default: info, choice: trace,debug,info,warn,error,fatal]
	      --log-type ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_TYPE)
	          Set the log type.
	          [default: text, choice: text,json]
	      --profile ($UNIKRAFT_PROFILE)
	          Set the current profile.
	      --[no-]telemetry ($UNIKRAFT_TELEMETRY)
	          Toggle anonymous usage analytics.
	          [default: true]
	      --version
	          Print version information.

$ unikraft certificate get --help

stdout:
	Inspect a certificate.

	Usage:
	  unikraft certificates get [<name> ...] [flags]

	Arguments:
	  [<name> ...]
	          Names of the certificates to inspect.

	Examples:
	  # Get a certificate by name or UUID
	  unikraft certificate get demo-cert

	Fields:
	  metro
	  name
	  uuid
	  common-name
	  subject
	  issuer
	  serial-number
	  state
